#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:794 port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:801
msgid "Cancelled: it stays as it was."
msgstr "Canceled: it stays as it was."

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:991
msgid "Cancelling: what it copied is removed…"
msgstr "Canceling: what it copied is removed…"

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:996
msgid "Cancelling: what was installed before is put back…"
msgstr "Canceling: what was installed before is put back…"

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1178
msgid "Cancelled. What it copied was removed, with any earlier copy of the same title: install it again to play it. Its saves are kept."
msgstr "Canceled. What it copied was removed, with any earlier copy of the same title: install it again to play it. Its saves are kept."

#: port/frontend/shell/pages.cpp:1181
msgid "Cancelled. What was installed before is as it was."
msgstr "Canceled. What was installed before is as it was."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:165
msgid "Frosted glass over each side's colours."
msgstr "Frosted glass over each side's colors."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:554
msgid "Bicubic is sharp, Bicubic Hermite a little softer, Bilinear softer still; Nearest neighbour keeps pixels square. AMD FSR 1 keeps edges clean for a game drawn below 4K, for a little more work by the GPU than Bicubic."
msgstr "Bicubic is sharp, Bicubic Hermite a little softer, Bilinear softer still; Nearest neighbor keeps pixels square. AMD FSR 1 keeps edges clean for a game drawn below 4K, for a little more work by the GPU than Bicubic."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:657
msgid "The 3DS's 3D screen as both eyes' pictures in one, red for the left and cyan for the right, to see in 3D with red and cyan glasses, as Azahar's anaglyph mode makes it, the 3D slider all the way up. Colours change with it. Applies to the next game."
msgstr "The 3DS's 3D screen as both eyes' pictures in one, red for the left and cyan for the right, to see in 3D with red and cyan glasses, as Azahar's anaglyph mode makes it, the 3D slider all the way up. Colors change with it. Applies to the next game."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1421
msgid "How the launcher looks: its colours, its corners and what moves behind the menus. Every theme has the same screens and buttons. Make your own as a JSON file in {0}/themes, starting from any of these: the text under this page says how. Only the launcher changes: the in-game menus and the games stay as they are."
msgstr "How the launcher looks: its colors, its corners and what moves behind the menus. Every theme has the same screens and buttons. Make your own as a JSON file in {0}/themes, starting from any of these: the text under this page says how. Only the launcher changes: the in-game menus and the games stay as they are."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1455
msgid "The focused game's picture fills the screen behind the menus, softened and dimmed, so moving the focus changes the whole screen. Off: the game's colours only."
msgstr "The focused game's picture fills the screen behind the menus, softened and dimmed, so moving the focus changes the whole screen. Off: the game's colors only."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1457
msgid "All, Recently added, Favourites: a row over the list."
msgstr "All, Recently added, Favorites: a row over the list."

#: port/frontend/shell/settings.cpp:1458
msgid "A row of filters over the Library's list: All, Recently added (the last 30 days), Favourites and, on the Wii U side, Graphic packs on, each with its count. Off: the list has every game, and Sort and Search are all it needs."
msgstr "A row of filters over the Library's list: All, Recently added (the last 30 days), Favorites and, on the Wii U side, Graphic packs on, each with its count. Off: the list has every game, and Sort and Search are all it needs."

